// Notation table for the milestone example. Demonstrates how to lay out a
// symbol legend. Bold symbols represent vectors, capital bold symbols
// represent matrices.

The following symbols recur throughout this report.

#table(
  columns: (auto, 1fr),
  align: (left, left),
  stroke: none,
  inset: (x: 6pt, y: 4pt),
  [$bold(x)$], [State vector],
  [$bold(A)$], [Linearized forward operator],
  [$sigma^2$], [Variance of the observation noise],
  [$mu$], [Posterior mean],
)

#v(6mm)
_Note._ Bold symbols represent vectors, capital bold symbols represent
matrices.
